//                      was re-papered into new equity, much smaller or junior
//                      debt, or a new loan. Never below pct_ever_na.
//                      Directionally comparable to Raymond James's
//                      "cumulative 1L default exposure" (ours spans all loans:
//                      equity, warrants, fund interests and vehicles are out
//                      of every curve; the _1l field gives the strictly
//                      comparable view: loans labelled first lien, one stop,
//                      unitranche, senior secured, senior loan or first out).
//   pct_ever_b80     = cumulative % ever marked < 80¢ on the dollar, among
//                      loans with a price mark by then (no par = left out).
//   pct_ever_modified= cumulative % with any modification event, among loans
//                      whose modification history could be judged
//                      (pct_mod_unknown = the share shown but left out;
//                      mod_partial when it is >= 5%). Null when nothing
//                      could be judged.
//   pct_b90_alive    = % of the cost observed at age T that has a price mark
