//                      that marked cost as % of all cost observed at age T.
//   pct_surviving    = % of eligible entry cost still on the book at age T
//                      (seen at age T or later), chained over the loans shown
//                      by each age. A late piece that starts at the holder's
//                      next filing after a piece of the same borrower and
//                      cohort ended (within 2x) continues that piece. Never
//                      above 100%; null when no loan is shown at age 0.
//
// is_partial: the vintage predates most of our filing coverage (survivors only).
//
// High-confidence (_hc) fields are published only when the HIGH+MED subset
// has 15+ eligible loans AND carries at least 25% of the counted cost
// (hc_cost_share). A figure resting on a sliver of the cohort is null. The
// first-lien (_1l) fields need 10+ first-lien loans. Neither is published where
// the all-dated figure is null; an age that fails these tests is null and the
// series goes on, unless a new event lands on it.
// cohort_estimated_b = cost of loans dated by an ESTIMATE (nearby tranche, name
// match, sibling facility, tenor model, holder's earlier position).
// cohort_first_seen_b = cost dated by first sighting, an observation rather than
// an estimate. cohort_low_tier_b also includes disclosed dates that drifted and
